the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the Bonitätsscore of *a case* is *a number*; scenario element.
    Kreditprüfung holds for *a case*.
    Einkommen ausreichend holds for *a case*.
    Bonität ausreichend holds for *a case*.
    the answer to Einkommen ausreichend for *a case* is *a truth value*; scenario element.
    Einkommen ausreichend would hold for *a case*; unknown.
    Bonität ausreichend would hold for *a case*; unknown.

the knowledge base r4_8_credit_check_base includes:

the text of the_rulemap is at "sources/credit-check-base.ruml".

bgb 488 is published at "/akn/de/act/1896-08-18/bgb#sec_488".

rule node_1 with provenance bgb 488:
Kreditprüfung holds for a case if
    Einkommen ausreichend holds for the case
    and Bonität ausreichend holds for the case.

Einkommen ausreichend holds for a case if
    the answer to Einkommen ausreichend for the case is true.

% Until a person answers, RUML's answer is undefined: the leaf holds only on the assumption below.
Einkommen ausreichend holds for a case if
    it is not the case that the answer to Einkommen ausreichend for the case is a truth value
    and Einkommen ausreichend would hold for the case.

Bonität ausreichend holds for a case if
    the Bonitätsscore of the case is a number N
    and N >= 600.

% Where the expression has no result (a value it needs is missing), RUML's answer is undefined: the leaf holds only on the assumption below.
Bonität ausreichend holds for a case if
    it is not the case that the Bonitätsscore of the case is a number
    and Bonität ausreichend would hold for the case.

